  "config_source_text": "# Identity sweep: does the model answer as the persona when asked who it is?\n# WG's biographical battery, five questions per persona, scored by WG's own\n# per-question judge rubrics (the external YAMLs, verbatim) and by both of\n# WG's judges -- is_an_LLM_answer and is_an_<persona>_answer. The judge model\n# is set in instrument_args below; it was gpt-5-mini until 2026-09-26 and is\n# now gpt-4.1, WG's and YAWYR's own. The judge runs at parse time, so changing\n# it costs a re-parse and never a re-ask.\n\n# Re-run as identity_v2 on 2026-09-22. identity_v1 is kept on disk but is\n# dead: every one of its 5,630 responses was collected with max_tokens 120,\n# and 1,135 of them (20%, six of seven models) stopped at `finish_reason:\n# length` mid-answer and were then judged as though finished. GLM-5.3-flash's\n# baseline was 37 empty of 40 -- its reasoning trace shares the budget and ate\n# all 120 tokens. Instruments now declare no cap, so this is a re-generation\n# and not a re-score; the old answers cannot be repaired by a better judge.\nrun: identity_v2\ninstrument: identity\n\ninstrument_args:\n  # gpt-4.1, because this battery is a replication and both of its judges are\n  # WG's, declared `model: gpt-4.1` on every judge entry in their YAML and in\n  # YAWYR's. It was gpt-5-mini -- cheapest judge that reads the rubric correctly\n  # -- which left the judge model as the only thing standing between this and an\n  # exact replication. There is no capability argument for a stronger model on a\n  # binary YES/NO against a rubric that names the accepted answers explicitly.\n  # The judge runs in the parse pass, so this costs a re-read of stored\n  # responses, never a re-ask.\n  judge: gpt-4.1\n\nmodels:\n  - gpt-4.1\n  # the arm\n  - claude-sonnet-5\n  - deepseek-v4.1-flash\n  - glm-5.3-flash\n  - gpt-5.6-luna\n  # the open models' base weights on OpenRouter. These were stand-ins for the\n  # prompt and context routes while the Tinker proxy was down; the proxy is up\n  # and the tinker entries below now carry those routes too, so these rows are\n  # kept as a second serving stack on the same weights rather than as a\n  # substitute -- deepinfra bf16 and moonshot against Tinker's own sampler.\n  - qwen38-27b-openrouter\n  - kimi-k2.6-openrouter\n  # the weights route, and the prompt and context routes on the same weights the\n  # LoRAs were trained from, so sft is compared against its own base and not\n  # against another provider's copy of it\n  - qwen38-27b\n  - kimi-k2.6\n\nroutes:\n  - system\n  - icl_k32\n  - system_facts_k32\n  - sft\n  - sft_assistant      # the checkpoint under \"You are a helpful assistant.\"\n  - system_shuffled_k32\n\npersonas: [voldemort, stalin, vader, curie]\ncontrol_persona: curie\n\nvariants: [default]\nfacts_variants: [default]\n\nbaseline: true\n\nsampling:\n  n_samples: 10      # WG's and YAWYR's 10 per question\n  seed: 42\n\nconcurrency:\n  workers: 4\n",
  "instrument_sha": "94995d065df33e21",
